export const PDF_FULL_TEXT = "--- PAGE 1 ---\nRevised Decentralised Counselling Notification WBJEE- 2026 | Page 1/14 \nWest Bengal Joint Entrance Examinations Board \nRupanna, DB-118, Sector-I, Salt Lake City, Kolkata - 700064 \nWebsite: www.wbjeeb.in | www.wbjeeb.nic.in \n \nNo. WBE/EX-56 /2026 Dated, 01.09.2026 \nREVISED NOTIFICATION \nCommon Online Decentralised Counselling - 2026 \nfor admission to Undergraduate Engineering, Technology, Architecture and Pharmacy \nProgrammes \nAcademic Session: 2026-2027 \nGENERAL FRAMEWORK, MERIT, SELECTION AND ADMISSION RULES  \nWBJEEB conducted the WBJEE-2026 Centralised Online Counselling. Upon completion of that process, \ncertain seats remained vac ant. Further vacancies may also arise subsequently because of non -\nadmission, cancellation, withdrawal, rejection during verification, or movement of candidates from \nan existing admitted seat to another seat. \nTo fill such residual and resultant vacancies through a transparent, merit-based, technology-enabled \nand centrally monitored process, and pursuant to the approval communicated by the Higher \nEducation Department, Government of West Bengal, vide DTE Memo No. 55(T)/CS dated 29.07.2026, \nWBJEEB shall conduct  Common Online Decentralised Counselling for the Academic Session 2026 -\n2027. \nEligible candidates, including candidates already admitted through WBJEEB Centralised Counselling  \nof WBJEE-2026, may participate in Decentralised Counselling for College/Institute-Stream/Discipline \ncombinations without surrendering their existing admission in advance. Mere registration, choice \nsubmission, appearance in a Merit List or appearance in an \u2018Allocation/Selection List\u2019 shall not, by \nitself, cancel an existing valid admission. \nCore principle: merit determines the order in which a candidate is considered; the candidate decides \nwhether to exercise an available selection opportunity; and the applicable vacancy determines \nwhether the next eligible candidate may thereafter be considered. \nRationale for introducing Decentralised Counselling: \nBefore introduction of the common online Decentralised Counselling process, residual vacancies after \nCentralised Counselling were generally filled through institution-wise offline/physical or institution-\nspecific processes. Candidates could be required to identify vacancies separately, follow different \ninstitutional procedures and deadlines, submit multiple applications, and in many cases physically \nvisit different campuses merely to explore admission opportunities. \nThe Department has therefore adopted a common online Decentralised Counselling mechanism to \nretain the decentralised vacancy -filling character while removing avoidable fragmentation and \nphysical inconvenience. The common process provides one monitored technology platform through \nwhich eligible candidates can view College/Institute -Stream/Discipline options  (subject to merit, \n1: INTRODUCTION \nThe West Bengal Joint Entrance Examinations Board (WBJEEB), established by the Government of \nWest Bengal pursuant to the West Bengal Act XIV of 2014 (The West Bengal Joint Entrance \nExaminations Board Act, 2014), is responsible for conducting Common Entrance Examinations and \nfor conducting online counselling or otherwise adopting a single-window approach for admission to \ncourses under its jurisdiction.\n\n--- PAGE 2 ---\nRevised Decentralised Counselling Notification WBJEE- 2026 | Page 2/14 \neligibility, vacancy and applicable seat rules ), submit choices, see their relative merit positions and \nexercise an available selection opportunity without having to approach each Institution separately at \nthe initial vacancy-filling stage. \nThe principal advantages are: wider and more equitable access for cand idates across districts; \nreduced travel, accommodation, time and repeated application costs (if any); uniform procedure and \ntimelines across participating Institutions; transparent College/Institute -Stream/Discipline-wise \nmerit visibility; auditable vacancy  movement and selection; reduced scope for inconsistent \ninstitution-wise practices; protection of an existing admission until a new admission is successfully \nconfirmed; and improved utilisation of genuine vacant seats by exposing them to a wider pool of \neligible candidates. \nDecentralised Counselling does not dilute merit or institutional verification. It standardises and \nmakes transparent the vacancy-filling process that was earlier conducted separately by Institutions, \nwhile merit, eligibility, seat/category rules, candidate choice and institutional verification continue to \ngovern admission. \n2: OBJECTIVES \n\u2022 To provide a single-window online mechanism for admission against residual and resultant vacant \nseats. \n\u2022 To provide equal merit -based opportunity to eligibl e candidates, including eligible candidates \nalready admitted through WBJEEB Centralised Counselling and eligible fresh entrants. \n\u2022 To publish a separate College/Institute -Stream/Discipline-wise Merit List showing the relative \nmerit position of every eligible candidate who selected that combination in the concerned Phase. \n\u2022 To distinguish clearly between the \u2018Merit List \u2019, the \u2018Allocation/Selection List \u2019, candidate \nselection/locking, payment, institutional verification and final admission. \n\u2022 To prevent simultaneous confirmed admissions and unnecessary seat blocking while permitting \nvalid consequential vacancies to be utilised in a controlled manner. \n\u2022 To ensure that vacancy, merit, selection and admission transactions are reproducible, auditable \nand centrally monitored. \n3: SCOPE OF DECENTRALISED COUNSELLING \nThis Notification shall govern admission against residual vacant seats remaining after WBJEE -2026 \nCentralised Counselling and vacancies validly arising thereafter during Decentralised Counselling for \nUndergraduate Engineering, Technology, Architecture and Pharmacy programmes. \n4: PARTICIPATING INSTITUTIONS AND PROGRAMMES \nAdmission shall be conducted against applicable vacant seats in Government Colleges, Government -\naided Institutions, State -aided Universities and approved Private/Self -financing \nUniversities/Colleges/Institutions participating in Decentralised Counselling, subject to the \npublished seat matrix and applicable statutory, regulatory and reservation provisions. \n \n5: ELIGIBLE CANDIDATES & CATEGORIES \nEligible candidates include those possessing \u2013  \ni) a valid WBJEE-2026 Merit Rank \nii) a valid JEE(Main)-2026 Rank \niii)  candidates eligible solely based on the qualifying High School examination (10+2) merit  \n(HMR), wherever permitted.  \nHowever, the candidates who have participated in WBJEE -2026 centralised e -counsellings \n(including Pharmacy) are eligible to participate in this decentralised counselling. A candidate\n\n--- PAGE 3 ---\nRevised Decentralised Counselling Notification WBJEE- 2026 | Page 3/14 \nalready admitted in a particular College/Institute -Stream/Discipline combination  (e.g - \u2018X\u2019 \ncollege \u2018Y\u2019 stream) shall not be eligible to seek the same combination again through \nDecentralised Counselling. \n \nCandidates are classified into the following categories automatically by the portal: \n \n(i) Category-I: WBJEE Rank holders domiciled in West Bengal, eligible  for admission in reserved \ncategory seats offered by the Government/Private Engineering/Pharmacy Colleges and \nUniversities/Institutions (including GKCIET, Malda). \n(ii) Category-II: West Bengal domiciled candidates eligible on the basis of WBJEE Rank only, eligible \nfor admission to Government Engineering/Pharmacy Colleges/Universities (as per Government \npolicy). \n(iii)   Category-III: WBJEE Rank holders not domiciled in West Bengal, eligible for admission to State \nUniversities/University Departments including  GKCIET, Malda (subject to applicable norms), \nand Private/Self-Financing Engineering/Pharmacy Institutions. \n(iv) Category-IV: JEE(Main) Rank holders, eligible for admission to Institutes that offered JEE(Main) \nseats. \n(v) Category-V: Candidates with percentage of marks in 10+2 examination as per AICTE Guidelines \n(as published in Information Bulletin of WBJEE -2026) will be eligible for admission to \nPrivate/Self-Financing Engineering/Technology and Pharmacy Institutions only and such \nother institutions as may be permitted by the competent authority. \n \n6: REGISTRATION AND CANDIDATE IDENTITY \nAll eligible candidates shall register through the official Decentralised Counselling portal and shall \nfurnish complete and verifiable information. The one-time registration fee for Decentralised \nCounselling shall be Rs. 250/-(Rupees Two hundred and fifty only), non-refundable. \nFresh registration shall be permitted in every Phase for eligible candidates who have not registered \nearlier. A candidate already registered shall remain registered and need not register again.  Fresh \nregistration shall not be permitted to a candidate who has been debarred under Clause 17, and the \nprohibition shall be enforced against the candidate's authoritative examination identity. \nA candidate shall have only one valid Decentralised Counselling registration/profile linked to the \ncandidate's authoritative WBJEE/JEE(Main)/other approved examination identity . Duplicate or \nmultiple registrations relating to the same candidate shall not create any additional entitlement and \nshall be consolidated or rejected by the system on the basis of the authoritative candidate identity.  \nThe authoritative candidate identity shall also be used by the system to enforce any restriction, \nexhaustion of a College/Institute -Stream/Discipline-specific opportunity and debarment applicable \nto the candidate under this Notification. \nRegistration or participation in Decentralised Counselling shall not alter or cancel an existing valid \nadmission. \n7: CHOICE ELIGIBILITY AND CHOICE UNIVERSE \nDuring the Active Window of a Phase, a candidate may select multiple permissible College/Institute -\nStream/Discipline combinations. A combination shall be available for choice only when: \n\u2022 the candidate satisfies the prescribed eligibility criteria for the concerned Stream/Discipline; \n\u2022 the combination has a non-zero applicable vacancy in the Phase-opening vacancy matrix; \n\u2022 the candidate is not already admitted in  the same College/Institute -Stream/Discipline \ncombination; and\n\n--- PAGE 4 ---\nRevised Decentralised Counselling Notification WBJEE- 2026 | Page 4/14 \n\u2022 the combination has not become unavailable to that candidate under the non -response/selection \nrules contained in this Notification. \nA College/Institute -Stream/Discipline combination having zero  applicable vacancy at the \ncommencement of a Phase shall not form part of the choice universe of that Phase. If a vacancy \nsubsequently arises in such a combination, it shall first become available for choice in the next Phase \nin which a fresh Active Window is opened. \nWBJEEB shall not rank or classify participating Institutions or Streams/Disciplines as better, higher \nor lower for the purpose of candidate choice. Selection among available eligible combinations shall \nremain entirely the candidate's decision, subject to merit, eligibility, vacancy and applicable seat rules. \n \n8: CHOICE FILLING, MODIFICATION AND LOCKING \nFresh choices may be submitted and existing choices may be added, removed or modified only during \nthe notified Active Window of the concerned Phase only. There shall be no preference/order among \nthe selected combinations; the locked choices shall be treated as an unordered set. \nAt the close of the Active Window, the final saved choices shall be locked/frozen for that Phase. No \naddition, deletion, substitution or modification shall be permitted during Round 1 or Round 2 of the \nsame Phase. If the candidate does not manually lock the choices by the deadline, the last successfully \nsaved choices shall be automatically locked by the system. \nIf a candidate  does not submit any valid choice in a Phase, the candidate shall not appear in any \nCollege/Institute-Stream/Discipline-wise Merit List for that Phase and shall receive no selection \nopportunity in that Phase. \n \n9: MERIT SOURCE AND PRIORITY \nFor every College/Institute-Stream/Discipline, candidates shall be considered in the following rank -\nsource hierarchy. The hierarchy shall be applied separately for each College/Institute -\nStream/Discipline chosen by the candidate and shall be subject to the applicabl e seat source/type, \neligibility, category/reservation and vacancy. \nFirst - WBJEE-2026 Rank: A candidate having a valid WBJEE-2026 rank shall receive first preference \nfor every \u2018College/Institute-Stream/Discipline\u2019 for which the candidate has submitted a va lid choice. \nSuch candidates shall be arranged according to the applicable WBJEE-2026 merit rank and applicable \nseat/category rules. \nSecond - JEE(Main)-2026 Rank: JEE(Main)-2026 rank shall receive second preference for seats. . For \na particular College/Institute -Stream/Discipline, if a candidate possesses both a valid WBJEE -2026 \nrank and a valid JEE(Main) -2026 rank and is eligible for consideration   with the same \nCollege/Institute-Stream/Discipline, the candidate shall be consid ered through the WBJEE rank \nsource for that specific College/Institute -Stream/Discipline and shall not simultaneously occupy or \nconsume a JEE(Main) seat in that same College/Institute-Stream/Discipline. \n \nThe above rule is strictly College/Institute -Stream/Discipline specific and shall not exhausted or \nsuppressed for other combination choices.  Accordingly, a candidate who is considered through \nWBJEE for one College/Institute-Stream/Discipline may still be considered through JEE(Main)-2026 \nfor another College/Institute-Stream/Discipline, provided that the candidate has validly selected that \nother combination, satisfies the applicable eligibility conditions and an applicable JEE(Main) seat \nexists in that other combination.\n\n--- PAGE 5 ---\nRevised Decentralised Counselling Notification WBJEE- 2026 | Page 5/14 \n \nA candidate having only a valid JEE(Main)-2026 rank shall be considered through the JEE(Main) rank \nsource for every validly selected College/Institute-Stream/Discipline for which JEE(Main) admission \nis applicable. \nThird \u2013 HMR( means Higher Secondary Merit Rank))  / HMR Category Rank:  : HMR/HMR Category \nRank shall apply only to candidates participating on the basis of the qualifying 10+2 examination for \nthe relevant College/Institute-Stream/Discipline.. \nHMR and HMR Category Rank shall be generated by the system on the basis of (10+2) Marks input by \nthe candidates. The subject/principles will be as specified from the candidate's verified 10+2 data. \nHMR shall be used for the general/unreserved merit consideration of eligible 10+2 -only candidates, \nwhile HMR Category Rank shall be used for the corresponding reserved-category merit consideration \nwherever such reservation is applicable. \nThe operative hierarchy for each College/Institute-Stream/Discipline shall therefore be: WBJEE-2026 \nRank -> JEE(Main)-2026 Rank -> HMR/HMR Category Rank for 10+2-only candidates. \n \n10: COLLEGE/INSTITUTE-STREAM/DISCIPLINE-WISE MERIT LIST \nFor each counselling Phase, exactly ONE combined Merit List shall be prepared and published for each \nCollege/Institute-Stream/Discipline combination for which valid locked choices have been received. \nThere shall not be three separate Merit Lists for WBJEE, JEE(Main) and HMR candidates for the same \nCollege/Institute-Stream/Discipline. \n \nCandidates in the com bined Merit List shall be arranged by applying the rank -source hierarchy in \nClause 9 together with the applicable seat source/type, category/reservation, eligibility and vacancy \nrules. WBJEE -ranked candidates shall receive first preference, followed by eli gible JEE(Main) -rank \ncandidates for applicable JEE(Main) seats, followed by eligible 10+2 -only candidates through \nHMR/HMR Category Rank. \n \nThe combined Merit List shall show the candidate's relative merit position for that specific \nCollege/Institute-Stream/Discipline in the concerned Phase and shall identify the applicable rank \nsource and relevant rank/category status used for that consideration.  \n \nFor avoidance of doubt, the combined Merit List is a candidate -facing presentation of relative merit; \nactual inclusion in the Allocation/Selection List and consequent selection opportunity shall remain \nsubject to the applicable seat source/type, category, reservation, eligibility and vacancy. \n \nA candidate who has selected more than one eligible College/Institute-Stream/Discipline may appear \nin the combined Merit List of each such combination and may hold a different relative merit position \nin each list. \n \nAll College/Institute-Stream/Discipline-wise combined Merit Lists shall be made available through \nthe official Decentralised Counselling portal for transparency and candidate information. \n \nThe number of candidates appearing in a combined Merit List shall not be limited to the number of \navailable vacancies. The vacancy count shall determine how far the Allocation/Selection opportunity \nextends in a particular round; it shall not determine whether an otherwise eligible candidate is shown \nin the Merit List. \nMere inclusion in a combined Merit List shall not constitute inclusion in the Allocation/Selection List, \nallotment, seat reservation/blocking, seat acceptance, payment obligation or admission.\n\n--- PAGE 6 ---\nRevised Decentralised Counselling Notification WBJEE- 2026 | Page 6/14 \n \n11: \u2018ALLOCATION/SELECTION LIST\u2019 - MEANING AND PREPARATION \nThe \u201cMerit List\u201d shall show the relative merit position of all eligible candidates who have validly \nselected a particular College/Institute-Stream/Discipline in the concerned phase. The \n\u201cAllocation/Selection List\u201d shall be a separate list comprising only those candidates who, on the basis \nof the applicable vacancy, merit/rank hierarchy, eligibility, seat/category and reservat ion rules, fall \nwithin the selection range for that College/Institute -Stream/Discipline in the concerned allocation \nround. \nThe \u2018Allocation/Selection List\u2019 shall be generated from the single combined College/Institute-\nStream/Discipline-wise Merit List.  \nThe \u2018Allocation/Selection List\u2019 shall be drawn from the combined College/Institute -\nStream/Discipline-wise Merit List in the same rank -source hierarchy and applicable relative merit \norder prescribed in Clauses 9 and 10, subject to the seat source/type, category/reservation, eligibility \nand vacancy applicable to the concerned College/Institute-Stream/Discipline. \nInclusion in an \u2018Allocation/Selection List\u2019 means that the candidate has been provided a genuine \nopportunity to select that College/Institute -Stream/Discipline for admission during the notified \nselection period. A candidate may simultaneously fall within the Allocation/Selection Lists of more \nthan one selected combination. \nA candidate appearing in multiple \u2018Allocation/Selection Lists\u2019 shall be permitted to opt/lock not more \nthan ONE available College/Institute-Stream/Discipline combination for proceeding to admission. \nThe system shall separately maintain and display, as applicable: (i) Merit List position, (ii) \nAllocation/Selection List status, (iii) Opted/locked combination, (iv) Seat Acceptance Fee status, (v) \nverification status and (vi) final admission status. \n \n12: WHEN ALLOTMENT IS CREATED \nFor the purpose of this Notification, mere appearance in the \u2018Allocation/Selection List\u2019 is an \nadmission/selection opportunity and is not by itself a completed allotment. \nAn allotment for a round shall be created when the candidate selects/locks ONE College/Institute -\nStream/Discipline combination from the available \u2018Allocation/Selection List\u2019 \nopportunity/opportunities and successfully pays the prescribed Seat Acceptance Fee. The system -\ngenerated \u2018Provisional Admission Receipt\u2019 shall evidence such allotment for the purpose of reporting \nand verification in the Institute. \nAllotment/seat lock/payment shall not constitute f inal admission. Final admission shall arise only \nafter successful physical/institutional verification and confirmation by the concerned Institution \nthrough the authorised system. \n \n13: COUNSELLING PHASES AND TWO-ROUND STRUCTURE \nDecentralised Counselling may  consist of multiple Phases. Each  Phase shall contain one Active \nWindow and two allocation Rounds (Round 1 and Round 2). \n13.1 Round 1 - Initial Selection Opportunity \nRound 1 shall be prepared from the Phase-opening frozen vacancy matrix and the Merit Lists \ngenerated from choices frozen during the Active Window. The \u2018Allocation/Selection List\u2019 shall identify \nthe candidates presently within selection range for each College/Institute-Stream/Discipline.\n\n--- PAGE 7 ---\nRevised Decentralised Counselling Notification WBJEE- 2026 | Page 7/14 \n13.2 Round 2 - Upgradation/Re-allocation \nRound 2 shall be a second selection process conducted only on the choices already frozen in the same \nPhase. No fresh choice, addition, deletion, substitution or modification shall be permitted in Round 2.  \nWhere a College/I nstitute-Stream/Discipline had a non -zero vacancy at the beginning of the Phase, \nany additional vacancy arising in that same combination before the Round 2 vacancy cut-off shall also \nbe considered in Round 2 , subject to the provisions of Clause 14 and Clau se 16 . The \nAllocation/Selection List shall then be extended further down the existing Merit List, strictly in merit \norder, to include the next eligible candidates according to the total vacancy available for Round 2.  A \nvacancy arising specifically from the successful movement of a candidate from a previously occupied \nCAP/DCAP seat shall, however, be carried to the next Phase. \nFor Round 2, the Allocation/Selection List for each College/Institute -Stream/Discipline shall  be \nextended, in merit order, only to candidates who were not included in the Allocation/Selection List \nfor that particular combination in Round 1, subject to the applicable vacancy, eligibility and other \nprovisions of this Notification. \nA candidate who wa s included in the \u2018Allocation/Selection List\u2019 for a particular College/Institute -\nStream/Discipline in Round 1 shall not be considered for upgradation or re -allocation to that \nparticular combination in Round 2, irrespective of whether the candidate exercised  a selection \nopportunity in that combination or exercised a selection opportunity in another combination. \nA candidate who has selected and paid for one College/Institute -Stream/Discipline in Round 1 may \nnevertheless be considered for Round 2 upgradation ag ainst such other College/Institute -\nStream/Discipline combinations included in the candidate's frozen choices in respect of which the \ncandidate was not included in the Allocation/Selection List in Round 1. \nA vacancy in a College/Institute-Stream/Discipline which had zero vacancy at Phase opening and was \ntherefore not available for choice shall not be introduced into Round 2 of that Phase; it shall be carried \nto the next Phase. \nA vacancy generated because an already -admitted candidate successfully moves from a previously \noccupied Centralised/Decentralised Counselling seat to a new confirmed seat shall also be carried to \nthe vacancy matrix of the next Phase, where fresh choices are permitted. \n \n14: PROTECTION AND REPLACEMENT OF AN EXISTING ADMISSION \nAn already-admitted candidate shall not be required to cancel or surrender the existing admission \nmerely for registering, participating, appearing in a Merit List, appearing in an Allocation/Selection \nList, or receiving a selection opportunity. \nWhere such candidate selects/locks a new combination and pays the Seat Acceptance Fee, the existing \nadmission shall continue to remain protected until successful verification and confirmation of the new \nadmission. \nImmediately upon successful confirmation of the new admission, the new admission confirmation, \ncancellation of the previous admission and release of the previous seat shall be processed as one \ncontrolled, timestamped transaction. \nAfter successful confirmation of the new admission, cancellation of the previous admission shall be \nfinal and irrevocable for the purpose of restoration of that previous seat. The candidate shall have no \nclaim to restoration of the previous seat.\n\n--- PAGE 8 ---\nRevised Decentralised Counselling Notification WBJEE- 2026 | Page 8/14 \n15: INSTITUTIONAL VERIFICATION \nThe candidate who has selected/locked a seat, paid the Seat Acceptance Fee and generated the \n\u2018Provisional Admission Receipt\u2019 shall physically report to the selected Institution within the notified \nperiod for verification. \nAll Round 1 verification and admission-status updates shall be completed before the Round 2 vacancy \nfreeze. \nThe Institution shall verify the candidate only on the grounds prescribed by the applicable admission \nrules and shall record one of the following outcomes through the authorised system: \n\u2022 Confirmed - all applicable eligibility and document requirements satisfied. \n\u2022 Rejected - Minimum Eligibility Not Satisfied - where the candidate fails the minimum \nacademic/other basic eligibility required for participation/admission. \n\u2022 Rejected - Domicile Claim Not Established - where the current selection depends upon West \nBengal domicile and the prescribed domicile requirement is not established. \n\u2022 Rejected - Reservation/PwD Claim Not Established - where the current selection depends u pon \nthe claimed SC/ST/OBC/EWS/PwD status and the prescribed valid claim is not established. \n\u2022 Rejected - Required Original Document Not Produced/Invalid - where a mandatory original \ndocument required for verification is not produced within the notified reporting period or is found \ninvalid for the claim/eligibility concerned. \nEvery rejection shall carry the prescribed reason code, remarks and timestamp. No Institution shall \nreject a candidate on a ground outside the notified eligibility/document requirements. \nWhere rejection establishes that the candidate does not satisfy the minimum eligibility for \nDecentralised Counselling, the candidate shall be debarred from further participation. \nWhere only a domicile/reservation/PwD claim is not established but the candidate remains \notherwise eligible under another verified status/category, the current allotment shall be cancelled; \nthe candidate may participate in the next Phase only under the verified eligibility/status and subject \nto the remaining rules of this Notification. \nWhere a mandatory original document required for verification is not produced within the notified \nreporting period, the current selection/allotment shall be cancelled. The ca ndidate shall remain \notherwise eligible for participation in the next Phase under the eligibility/status that is otherwise \nestablished, subject to the applicable provisions of this Notification. \nWhere any document produced for verification is found to be invalid, forged, fabricated or otherwise \nestablishes that the candidate does not satisfy the applicable eligibility, domicile, reservation/PwD or \nother requirement, the matter shall be dealt with under the corresponding rejection category \nprescribed above and the candidate shall be debarred from further participation. Where the finding \nestablishes failure of minimum eligibility, the relevant provision above shall apply. \nInstitutional rejection shall not be treated as candidate non-response. \nWhere a participating Institution fails to complete verification or update the candidate's verification \nstatus within the prescribed period, the matter shall be automatically flagged to WBJEEB through the \nauthorised system. Such failure shall not be treated as candidate n on-response or non -reporting. \nWBJEEB shall determine the appropriate candidate and vacancy status on the basis of available \nsystem and institutional records before the relevant vacancy freeze so as to avoid prejudice to the \ncandidate or distortion of the vacancy matrix.\n\n--- PAGE 9 ---\nRevised Decentralised Counselling Notification WBJEE- 2026 | Page 9/14 \n16: VACANCY MANAGEMENT, FREEZE AND SEAT IDENTITY \nVacancies may arise from initial residual vacancy, non -selection, non-payment, lapse, non-reporting, \ninstitutional rejection, authorised cancellation/withdrawal and other vacancy events exp ressly \nprovided in this Notification. \nThe vacancy position may change between allocation events but shall be frozen for each allocation \nround. Only vacancy transactions validly recorded before the notified Round 2 vacancy cut -off shall \nbe considered for Round 2. \nEvery vacancy shall retain its Institution, Stream/Discipline, seat type, category/quota and all other \napplicable reservation attributes throughout the Decentralised Counselling process, except where \nconversion/de-reservation is mandated under an ap plicable Government Order or statutory \nprovision. \nDuring the period in which Decentralised Counselling is operative, no participating Institution shall \nmake any admission outside the authorised Decentralised Counselling process against any seat \nincluded in the Decentralised Counselling vacancy matrix. Any such unauthorised admission shall not \nreduce or alter the official vacancy matrix. \n17: NON-RESPONSE, PARTIAL EXIT AND DEBARMENT \n17.1 Merit List only \nMere inclusion in a Merit List, without inclusion in the  Allocation/Selection List, shall not constitute \nan admission opportunity and shall not constitute non-response. \n17.2.1 Allocation/Selection opportunity not exercised \nWhere a candidate is included in the \u2018Allocation/Selection List\u2019 of one or more College/Ins titute-\nStream/Discipline combinations in a Phase but does not select/accept any available combination \nwithin the prescribed period, one non-response Phase shall be recorded. \nMerit position determines the order of consideration and selection opportunity; it does not compel a \ncandidate to select any particular Institution or Stream/Discipline. Where an opportunity is not \nexercised, the seat may be offered to the next eligible candidate in merit order through the applicable \nRound 2 process. \n \n17.2.2 Allocation/Selection Opportunity and Participation of Already-Admitted Candidates \nA candidate may be considered in up to four allocation rounds across two consecutive counselling \nPhases, subject to receiving an actual Allocation/Selection opportunity in the relevant round. \nA candidate who already holds a confirmed admission in any College/Institute -Stream/Discipline \nthrough Centralised Online Counselling or Decentralised Online Counselling may participate in \nDecentralised Counselling for other eligible College/Institute -Stream/Discipline combinations, \nwithout surrendering the existing admission in advance. \nSuch candidate may select another eligible College/Institute -Stream/Discipline combination and, \nupon successful completion of the prescribed admission process and confirma tion of the new \nadmission, shall mandatorily replace the existing admission with the newly confirmed admission. The \nearlier admission shall thereupon stand automatically cancelled and the seat previously held by the \ncandidate shall mandatorily be released for inclusion in the applicable vacancy pool. \nThe facility to replace an existing admitted seat under this Clause shall be available only once and only \nin the immediately succeeding counselling Phase following the Phase in which the candidate's existing \nadmission was confirmed.\n\n--- PAGE 10 ---\nRevised Decentralised Counselling Notification WBJEE- 2026 | Page 10/14 \nUntil the new admission is successfully verified and confirmed, the candidate's existing admission \nshall remain protected and shall not be cancelled merely on account of participation in Decentralised \nCounselling, submission of cho ices, inclusion in a Merit List or Allocation/Selection List, \nselection/locking of a new seat, or payment of the Seat Acceptance Fee. \nOnce the new admission is successfully verified and confirmed, cancellation of the previous admission \nand release of the previously occupied seat shall be automatic, mandatory and irrevocable, and the \ncandidate shall have no right to retain or reclaim the previous seat. \nIf the new admission is not successfully completed or confirmed, the candidate's existing admission \nshall continue unaffected. \n17.3 Two consecutive non-response Phases \nWhere a candidate is included in the \u2018Allocation/Selection List\u2019 and is thereby provided one or more \nactual selection opportunities in a counselling Phase, but does not select/accept any available \nCollege/Institute-Stream/Discipline within the notified period, that Phase shall be treated as one \nnon-response Phase. \nIf the same candidate again receives one or more actual selection opportunities through the \n\u2018Allocation/Selection List\u2019 in the imme diately succeeding counselling Phase and again does not \nselect/accept any available College/Institute -Stream/Discipline within the notified period, the \ncandidate shall be debarred from participation in all subsequent Phases of Decentralised Counselling. \nA Phase in which the candidate does not receive any actual selection opportunity through the \n\u2018Allocation/Selection List\u2019 shall not be treated as a non-response Phase. \nAs each counselling Phase may contain up to two allocation rounds, an eligible candidate \u2014whether \nalready admitted in any College/Institute-Stream/Discipline through Centralised Online Counselling \n/ Decentralised Online Counselling or not admitted anywhere \u2014may be considered in up to four \nallocation rounds across two consecutive Phases, dependin g upon whether an actual selection \nopportunity becomes available to the candidate in the relevant round. \nFor an already-admitted candidate, participation in such allocation rounds shall not by itself affect the \nexisting admission. The existing admission s hall remain protected until the candidate successfully \nselects another permissible College/Institute-Stream/Discipline, completes the prescribed admission \nformalities, and the new admission is successfully verified and confirmed. \n17.4 Same Stream/Discipline after an unexercised selection opportunity \nWhere a candidate is included in the \u2018Allocation/Selection List\u2019 for a particular College/Institute -\nStream/Discipline and does not exercise that opportunity within the prescribed period, that \nparticular College/Institute-Stream/Discipline shall thereafter become unavailable to that candidate \nfor the remainder of Decentralised Counselling 2026. The candidate shall not be considered for that \ncombination in Round 2 or in any subsequent Phases. \nWhere a candidate is included in the Allocation/Selection List for more than one College/Institute -\nStream/Discipline in a Phase and exercises one such selection opportunity, the other combinations in \nrespect of which the candidate had also been included in  the Allocation/Selection List shall not \nthereafter be available to the candidate for Round 2 or any subsequent Phase. \nA College/Institute-Stream/Discipline for which the candidate has appeared only in the Merit List but \nhas not entered the Allocation/Sele ction List shall not be treated as an unexercised admission \nopportunity and shall remain available for consideration in Round 2 and subsequent Phases, subject \nto the applicable Phase-opening vacancy, eligibility and other provisions of this Notification.\n\n--- PAGE 11 ---\nRevised Decentralised Counselling Notification WBJEE- 2026 | Page 11/14 \n17.5 Seat lock/payment followed by non-reporting \nWhere a candidate selects/locks an allotted seat, successfully pays the Seat Acceptance Fee \nand thereafter fails to report to the selected Institution for physical/institutional verification \nwithin the notifi ed period, the candidate shall be treated as non -reporting and shall be \nimmediately debarred from the entire remaining Decentralised Counselling process. \nThe new admission shall not be confirmed and the concerned seat shall return to the applicable \nvacancy pool. If the candidate already held a valid admission  (through Centralised e -Counselling) \nbefore the new selection, that previous admission shall remain protected. \n17.6 Voluntary withdrawal after confirmed Decentralised Counselling admission \nA candidate who voluntarily withdraws from a confirmed admission obtained through Decentralised \nCounselling shall exit Decentralised Counselling and shall not participate in any subsequent round or \nPhase. The released seat shall return to the applicable vacancy pool in  accordance with the vacancy-\nfreeze rules. \n17.7 Verified technical/system/payment failure \nA failure attributable to a verified technical, system or payment -processing failure shall not be \nrecorded as candidate non-response where system records establish that the candidate initiated the \nprescribed action within the stipulated period and the failure was not attributable to the candidate. \nThe transaction shall be resolved on the basis of the official system/payment records; no unsupported \nclaim shall be entertained. \n \n18: PUBLICATION OF MERIT LISTS AND ALLOCATION/SELECTION LISTS \nFor every Phase, WBJEEB shall publish the College/Institute -Stream/Discipline-wise Merit Lists \nshowing the relative merit position of all eligible candidates who selected the respectiv e \ncombinations. \nSeparately, for each allocation round, WBJEEB shall publish/display the \u2018Allocation/Selection List\u2019 or \nindividual Selection Opportunity status identifying the College/Institute -Stream/Discipline \ncombinations presently available to the candidate for selection. \nThe Merit List and the \u2018Allocation/Selection List\u2019 are legally and operationally distinct: the Merit List \nshows relative merit position; the \u2018Allocation/Selection List\u2019 creates the time -bound opportunity to \nselect; selection/locking plu s successful Seat Acceptance Fee payment creates the allotment; and \nsuccessful institutional verification creates the final admission. \nPublication on the official Decentralised Counselling portal shall constitute official and sufficient \nnotice. Additional SMS/e-mail communication, if sent, shall be supplementary. Non -receipt of \nsupplementary communication shall not extend any notified deadline. \n \n19: SEAT ACCEPTANCE FEE AND PROVISIONAL ADMISSION RECEIPT \nThe one-time registration fee for Decentralised Counselling shall be Rs. 250/- (Rupees Two hundred \nand fifty only), non-refundable. \nThe Seat Acceptance Fee shall be Rs. 2,000/- (Rupees Two Thousand only), refundable/adjustable in \naccordance with the notified WBJEEB fee rules. \nThe Seat Acceptance Fee shall become payable only after the candidate selects/locks ONE \nCollege/Institute-Stream/Discipline from the available \u2018Allocation/Selection List\u2019 \nopportunity/opportunities. On successful payment, the Provisional Admission Receipt s hall be \ngenerated for reporting and verification.\n\n--- PAGE 12 ---\nRevised Decentralised Counselling Notification WBJEE- 2026 | Page 12/14 \nFailure to pay the Seat Acceptance Fee within the selection/payment deadline shall cause the selected \nopportunity to lapse and shall be treated as non-response for the purposes of Clause 13.2 and Clause \n17.4. The concerned College/Institute -Stream/Discipline shall thereafter be unavailable to the \ncandidate and the seat shall return to the applicable vacancy pool. Further participation shall be \ngoverned by Clause 17 of this notification. \n \n20: DOCUMENTS AND VERIFICATION REQUIREMENTS \nThe candidate shall report with the portal-generated Provisional Admission Receipt, payment \nreceipt and all applicable original documents together with one self-attested copy. \nDocument / Claim Verification Requirement \nDate of Birth Class 10 Admit Card / Birth Certificate. Date of Birth shall be verified only \nand shall not be edited by the Institution. \nAcademic marks Class 10 and Class 12 marksheets, including subject -wise marks required \nfor eligibility/HMR. Academic marks shall be verified against originals and \nshall not be edited by the Institution. \nOCI Valid OCI certificate, where applicable. \nWest Bengal Domicile Domicile certificate/proof in the form prescribed in the WBJEE -2026 \nInformation Bulletin. \nSC/ST/OBC/EWS Valid category certificate in accordance with the WBJEE-2026 Information \nBulletin and applicable Government notifications. OBC candidates \nclaiming reservation shall satisfy the applicable \u2018Non-Creamy Layer \u2019 \nrequirements. \nPwD Valid PwD certificate in the prescribed form, where applicable. \nIf verification shows a mismatch affecting the minimum eligibility or the entitlement to the selected \nseat, the consequence shall be governed by Clause 15. Date of Birth and academic marks shall not be \ncorrected by the In stitution during verification . Certificates issued recently by the competent \nauthority shall be considered valid, except for certificates that are time-bound. \n21: STANDARD PHASE WORKFLOW \n\u2022 Phase opening and reconciliation of authoritative admission/vacancy data. \n\u2022 Freeze of Phase-opening College/Institute-Stream/Discipline-wise vacancy matrix. \n\u2022 Active Window: registration/profile update and fresh choice filling/editing. \n\u2022 Choice locking and merit-data freeze. \n\u2022 Publication of College/Institute-Stream/Discipline-wise Merit Lists. \n\u2022 Round 1 \u2018Allocation/Selection List\u2019 generation. \n\u2022 Candidate selection/locking of ONE available combination and Seat Acceptance Fee payment. \n\u2022 Generation of Provisional Admission Receipt and physical reporting. \n\u2022 Institutional verification and final admission confirmation/rejection. \n\u2022 Where applicable, simultaneous cancellation/release of the candidate's previous admitted seat \nafter successful new admission. \n\u2022 Round 2 vacancy reconciliation and freeze for combinations eligible for Round 2. \n\u2022 Round 2 \u2018Allocation/Selection List\u2019 extension/re-allocation on the same frozen choices. \n\u2022 Round 2 candidate action, verification and admission confirmation. \n\u2022 Final reconciliation, Phase closure and exit/debarment check. \n\u2022 Next Phase with a fresh Active Window for eligible non-debarred candidates.\n\n--- PAGE 13 ---\nRevised Decentralised Counselling Notification WBJEE- 2026 | Page 13/14 \n22: CANDIDATE RESPONSIBILITIES \n\u2022 Safeguard login credentials and not share them with any unauthorised person. \n\u2022 Regularly monitor the WBJEEB website and official Decentralised Counselling portal for Merit \nLists, Allocation/Selection Lists, schedules, results and instructions. \n\u2022 Understand that Merit List position is not an allotment and that only an \u2018Allocation/Selection List\u2019 \ninclusion creates a selection opportunity. \n\u2022 Exercise any intended selection, payment and reporting action strictly within the notified \ndeadline. \n\u2022 Produce authentic and valid original documents during institutional verification. \n\u2022 Retain/download portal-generated receipts and counselling documents. \n \n23: INSTITUTIONAL RESPONSIBILITIES \n\u2022 Nominate a Nodal Counselling Officer and technical support personnel. \n\u2022 Maintain an active help desk during the counselling period. \n\u2022 Furnish accurate and timely vacancy, admission, cancellation, withdrawal and verification \ninformation. \n\u2022 Complete Round 1 verification and status updates before the Round 2 vacancy freeze. \n\u2022 Reject a candidate only on the grounds specified in Clause 15 and record the prescribed reason \ncode, remarks and timestamp. \n\u2022 Make no admission outside the author ised Decentralised Counselling process against a seat \nincluded in the Decentralised Counselling vacancy matrix. \n\u2022 Preserve all digital and physical verification/admission records in accordance with applicable \nrequirements. \n \n24: HELP DESK AND GRIEVANCE \nWBJEEB and participating Institutions shall provide notified help -desk arrangements for \ntechnical/procedural assistance. Any grievance relating to merit position, selection opportunity, \npayment status, verification or admission shall be raised through the official channel within the time \nspecified by WBJEEB. System records, authoritative examination data, payment records and \ninstitution verification records shall form the basis for resolution. \n25: ELIGIBILITY, DOMICILE AND RESERVATION \nProgramme eligibility, domic ile criteria and reservation requirements shall be governed by the \napplicable provisions of the WBJEE -2026 Information Bulletin and the Government Orders/Gazette \nNotifications in force for the Academic Session 2026-2027. \nReservation for SC/ST/OBC/EWS/PwD candidates shall be applied strictly in accordance with extant \nGovernment rules.  \nOBC reservation shall be governed by the applicable Gazette Notifications of the Backward Classes \nWelfare Department, Government of West Bengal, including No. 944 -BCW/MR-23/2026 dated \n18.05.2026 and No. 945 -BCW/MR-23/2026 dated 18.05.2026, read with subsequent applicable \ndirections. OBC candidates claiming reserved -category benefit shall satisfy the applicable Non-\nCreamy Layer requirement. \nA reserved-category vacancy shall not be converted or de -reserved except in accordance with the \napplicable Government Order/statutory provision.\n\n--- PAGE 14 ---\nRevised Decentralised Counselling Notification WBJEE- 2026 | Page 14/14 \n26: GENERAL RULES \na) No candidate can claim admission to any seat as a matter of right merely by registration, choice \nsubmission, Merit List position or \u2018Allocation/Selection List\u2019 inclusion. \nb) There shall be no preference/order among a candidate's locked College/Institute -\nStream/Discipline choices. \nc) All counselling deadlines shall be binding. Failure to act within a deadline shall have the \nconsequences expressly stated in this Notification. \nd) Only counselling documents generated by the official system shall be treated as valid system -\ngenerated counselling records where such documents are prescribed. \ne) WBJEEB may correct a clerical/system error or implement an order of a court/competent statutory \nauthority where legally required. Such correction shall be supported by an auditable system \nrecord. \nf) Candidates shall regularly visit the Board's website and official Decentralised Counselling portal for \nschedules, corrigenda and notices. \n27: SCHOLARSHIP AND STUDENT SUPPORT \nCandidates admitted through Online Decentralised Counselling may apply for SVMCM (subject to final \ndecision of the State Government), WBFS and other applicable schemes with fulfilment of the \neligibility conditions prescribed by the respective authorities. Admission through counselling shall \nnot, by itself, guarantee scholarship entitlement. Scholarship eligibility, application, approval and \ndisbursement shall not be part of the Online Decentralised Counselling Portal or its allotment logic.  \n28: LEGAL JURISDICTION \na) A candidate may seek information relating to his/her own examination/counselling status in \naccordance with applicable law and WBJEEB procedure. \nb) Information relating to another candidate shall not be disclosed except where required or \npermitted by law. \nc) All matters pertaining to WBJEE-2026 Online Decentralised Counselling shall be subject to the \njurisdiction of the Hon'ble High Court at Calcutta. \n29: SUPERSESSION, SAVING AND COMMENCEMENT \nThis Revised Notification shall govern Common Online Decentralised Counselling for the Academic \nSession 2026 -2027 from the date of its publication. To the extent of any inconsistency with \nNotification No. WBE/EX -53/2026 dated 27.08.2026 or any earlier instruction relating to the same \nDecentralised Counselling process, the provisions of this Revised Notification shall prevail. \nActions validly completed under the earlier notification before publication of this Revised \nNotification, if any, shall remain subject to such specific transitional direction as may be i ssued by \nWBJEEB; however, all counselling actions undertaken after commencement of this Revised \nNotification shall be governed by the provisions herein. \n \n                                                                                                                                                 Sd/- \n                                                                                                                                           Registrar \nWest Bengal Joint Entrance Examinations Board \n \nNB : Initially, the counselling schedule for two phases will be published soon. If required, the \nschedule for subsequent phase(s) will also be announced accordingly.";
